{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed. Gerrit 3149 merged as `50d5a36539d` (pushed `bed4448e175`; Gerrit rebased server-side under Rebase-If-Necessary, so the merged SHA differs from the pushed one). `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`.\n\nAll 10 ACs measured green against the change:\n\n- AC1 `git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- src tests scripts` exits 1, no output.\n- AC2 `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md` absent.\n- AC3 `regenerate-index` exits 0 and leaves the committed index unchanged.\n- AC4 index object length 6 (5 reviewers + `_generated_by`), was 7.\n- AC5 `115 passed`, was 117.\n- AC6 collect-only diff vs `origin/main` is exactly two deletions —\n  `test_prompt_cache_split.py::test_marked_prompt_prefix_is_variable_free[ticket-quality]` and\n  `test_prompt_front_matter.py::test_built_in_prompt_round_trips_canonically[ticket-quality-path85]` —\n  with no other line changed. No `pathNN` suffix shifted, because `ticket-quality` sorted last.\n- AC7 diff lists exactly the 5 claimed paths.\n- AC8 `ruff check src tests docs` clean.\n- AC9 `docs/release-notes.md` 17 additions, 0 deletions.\n- AC10 `make verify` exit 0 — 19,837 passed, 90 skipped, 0:50:20.\n\n**One advisory finding from `LLM-Review`, verified correct and being fixed under this ticket rather than deferred.** `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py:157` — the section header above the golden round-trip block — still read \"the MIGRATED BUILT-IN prompts (the 6 reviewers)\". The slice updated the sibling count at :174 but missed this one, so the slice itself is what made it wrong. Follow-up commit `86ce31117e3` (\"Correct the reviewer count in a test comment\") corrects it to \"the 5 reviewers\"; `make verify` is running before that push. The ticket stays `in_progress` until that second change merges.\n\nOperational note for later slices: a `git merge-base --is-ancestor <pushed-sha> origin/main` mirror check can never succeed when Gerrit rebases. Read `current_revision` off the merged change and poll for *that* SHA instead — it appeared on the GitHub mirror about 1 minute after submit."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793376434387391846,"uuid":"317196e3-7333-4609-b0ec-2c40fbb56ee0"}